# Factory Vision, Docker build context
#
# The two Dockerfiles copy workspace manifests first and run `pnpm install`
# before copying sources, so a dependency install is cached across source
# edits. That only works if the host's own `node_modules` never enters the
# context: pnpm links every dependency as an absolute symlink into the local
# store (`/d/Master/Factory Vision/node_modules/.pnpm/…`), and a later
# `COPY packages packages` would drop those dangling links on top of the clean
# install the image just made. The build then fails on the first `tsc` with
# `Cannot find module …/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc`.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output is produced inside the image; copying the host's would either
# ship a stale bundle or defeat the build cache.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never reaches an image, and .git in particular is most of the context size.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
Docs
deploy/.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
coverage
.cache
.temp
.tmp-fonts
.pnpm-store
